[Music]  police are saying a murder and attempted  murder are  caught on camera the person recording  the alleged killer himself  it is a story you will only see here  first on 8 news now  the i-team obtained the evidence at the  center of the case  vanessa murphy now has a story that we  do want to warn you  this report does include disturbing  content  a walk to a man who appears to be  homeless and passed out on the sidewalk  an arm raised gun pointed and the  trigger pulled  the i-team is freezing the video before  the victim is shot  in the middle of the forehead this was  in the early morning hours of july 13th  then on july 15 just before midnight as  a 62-year-old man walks his dog he  describes a man dressed as a mummy  approaching him and shooting him in the  chest  two crime scenes two days apart both  locations near sahara and decatur in las  vegas  metro police call the first a murder the  victim  48 year old brent lloyd his body  discovered by a jogger  the second in attempted murder the  victim survived  and called 911 himself after he ran to  his nearby home  three months later he is recovering from  his injuries  investigators say surveillance video  helped them find their suspect by  tracking his path  twenty-one-year-old noah green lives in  a nearby apartment complex  on july 18 police say after he ran from  officers as they approached him they  found this gun on him  and this cell phone with only two videos  on it  these a detective testified in front of  the grand jury  he was shocked he said greene denied any  involvement in the crimes  when he showed green the videos he  didn't see any outward reaction  he said that's his phone but he didn't  know how the videos got there  his defense attorney is questioning his  mental status  referring to the arrest report police  noted he appeared to talk to himself  during surveillance detectives say  green's mother described him as a loner  and after he told police about a  girlfriend and they tried to find her  it appeared she didn't exist greene was  indicted by the grand jury  he faces seven charges and is currently  at the clark county detention center  held on no bail vanessa murphy  8 news now noah greene's next court  appearance is set for november 6.

